$DATUM Methyl 2-(4,5-bis(benzyloxy)picolinamido)acetate (INT-A): HATU (0.36 g,
0.96 mmol) and DIPEA (0.25 mL, 1.4 mmol) were added to a solution of
4,5-bis(benzyloxy)picolinic acid (0.27 g, 0.80 mmol) in DMF (2 mL). After
10 min, methyl 2-aminoacetate HCl salt (0.1 g, 0.80 mmol) was added. The
reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature overnight. The mixture
was diluted with EtOAc, washed with brine, concentrated, and purified by
silica gel column chromatography (0-100% EtOAc in hexanes). The product
as a clear oil (290 mg, 90%). 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d 6): δ ppm 8.90 (t,
1H), 8.30 (s, 1H), 7.70 (s, 1H), 7.34-7.38 (m, 10H), 5.33 (s, 4H), 4.0
(m, 2H), 3.64 (s, 3H). ESI-MS m/z: 407.0 [M + H]+.
